{
  "id": "binary-addition",
  "title": "Binary Addition: How the Carry Walks Left",
  "eyebrow": "digital arithmetic",
  "language": "en",
  "duration": 55,
  "topic": "Adding two 4-bit binary numbers column-by-column from the least significant bit up — the carry-out from one column slides left to become the carry-in of the next.",
  "subject_id": "ade",
  "chapter_number": 5,
  "prerequisites": [
    "hexadecimal-counting"
  ],
  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "manimoIntro",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 9.49,
      "narration": "Computers add the way you do — column by column, right to left, carrying when you overflow. The only difference is the alphabet has just two letters.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "center",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "manimo-enter",
            "content": "Manimo bobs in centre",
            "delay": 0
          },
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "Same long addition you learned in school — in base two.",
            "delay": 0.7,
            "color": "var(--chalk-100)",
            "position": "right of Manimo, serif italic"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "rules",
      "start": 9.49,
      "end": 22.61,
      "narration": "Four cases per column. Zero plus zero gives zero. Zero plus one gives one. One plus one — and now it overflows: the sum bit drops to zero and a carry pops out the top.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "center",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "text-title",
            "content": "PER-COLUMN RULES",
            "delay": 0.2,
            "color": "var(--amber-300)",
            "position": "centre top"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "0 + 0 = 0   (carry 0)",
            "delay": 0.7,
            "color": "var(--chalk-200)",
            "position": "row 1"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "0 + 1 = 1   (carry 0)",
            "delay": 1.5,
            "color": "var(--chalk-200)",
            "position": "row 2"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "1 + 1 = 0   (carry 1)",
            "delay": 3,
            "color": "var(--rose-300)",
            "position": "row 3 — the overflow row"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "1 + 1 + 1 = 1   (carry 1)",
            "delay": 4.5,
            "color": "var(--rose-300)",
            "position": "row 4 — with carry-in"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "two ones overflow base two — they always do",
            "delay": 6,
            "color": "var(--chalk-300)",
            "position": "bottom caption"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "walk",
      "start": 22.61,
      "end": 37.09,
      "narration": "Add zero one zero one and zero one one one, right to left. Each one plus one rolls over and a carry slides up to the next column. After four columns we land on one one zero zero — twelve in decimal.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "center",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "Two operands: 0101 and 0111, lined up vertically",
            "delay": 0.2,
            "color": "var(--chalk-200)",
            "position": "centre-top"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-path",
            "content": "Column cursor sweeps right-to-left, highlighting one column at a time",
            "delay": 1,
            "color": "var(--amber-400)"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-label",
            "content": "Sum bit fades in below each column as the cursor leaves it",
            "delay": 1,
            "color": "var(--chalk-100)"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-label",
            "content": "Carry token slides up-and-left from column i to column i+1",
            "delay": 1,
            "color": "var(--rose-400)"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "Decimal check: 5 + 7 = 12",
            "delay": 20,
            "color": "var(--amber-300)",
            "position": "below result"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "longestPath",
      "start": 37.09,
      "end": 47.74,
      "narration": "In hardware, that left-walking carry is the bottleneck. The most significant bit cannot settle until every carry below it has settled. The longest carry chain sets the clock.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "center",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "text-title",
            "content": "WHY HARDWARE CARES",
            "delay": 0.2,
            "color": "var(--amber-300)",
            "position": "centre top"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-path",
            "content": "Four FA blocks in a row with a carry chain animating LSB → MSB",
            "delay": 0.6,
            "color": "var(--chalk-200)"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-label",
            "content": "Carry line lights segment by segment from LSB to MSB",
            "delay": 0.6,
            "color": "var(--rose-400)"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "the longest carry chain sets the adder's worst-case delay",
            "delay": 4.5,
            "color": "var(--chalk-300)",
            "position": "below the chain"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "takeaway",
      "start": 47.74,
      "end": 55,
      "narration": "Same algorithm, different alphabet — and carries are how the columns talk to each other.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "center",
